Z||000003||ThatRickGuy||07-13-2000||07:19 AM||||When my car was running I knowticed it also, altho I don't think it ever really went away. I coun't hear it at traveling speed, but when I came up to a stop light or anything like that I could here it sucking away. I just assumed it was the ammount of air and they curvey design of the air intake. Of course when I was driving my engine was idleing a bit high. Watch the tack, maybe it goes away when your car drops to low idle.||||reg||1
Z||000004||BAM-BAM||07-13-2000||07:48 AM||||  Well, I hate to inform you guys that you have one of the most common problems known to the Fiero. I happens to virtually every V6 Fiero ever made and there is relatively little that can be done to correct it. I don't really know if this anomali occurs on the 4Cyl's. What happens is, every time you start the engine, there is a sort of butterfly valve in the throttle body that opens partially and it is directly proportional to the throttle position. this "partially" open valve creates a vortex of sorts going through the TB and intake which oddly enough has no harmful side effects. As a matter af fact, it has been proven to actually be some what of a neccessity. If by some chance, the pitch or audible level change, don't worry it may only be relative to mass air density. Heavier air is louder. That's about all I know with a relatively limited knowledge.<P><BR>  Late, BAM OUT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>P.S. It is the normal sound of the intake. <P>------------------<BR>Don B. <BR>85GT||||reg||12
Z||000005||Standard||07-13-2000||02:39 PM||||I love that little intake roar on startup, sounds pretty mean imho..<P>------------------<BR>Mike -- Golden Valley, MN<BR>Black 86.5 GT 5 Spd, 147,000 miles and counting!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/BURNOUT.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||theogre||07-13-2000||03:34 PM||||It's been making that sound right along. You just hear it more now because you redirected it toward the front with the scoop.<P>------------------<BR>Lake Superior? Is that what I stepped in? Sorry.||||reg||1
Z||000007||TheFiero64||07-13-2000||05:38 PM||||It is the sweet sound of the air entering the <B>IAC</B>(Idle Air Control) valve. The reason you here it so loud at startup is because the <B>IAC</B> is open more to give a fast warm-up idle.<P>------------------<BR>Joshua Bumpus<BR>New Bedford, MA<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fi.jpg"> ||||reg||6
